      "label": "Ratio notation and terms",
      "statements": [
        {
          "id": "pp3u2-1:prior-knowledge-1",
          "type": "prior_knowledge",
          "text": "We have learned in previous phases the subject of ratio, and that ratio is a comparison between two quantities.",
          "page": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "pp3u2-1:definition-1",
          "type": "definition",
          "text": "The ratio between two numbers a and b can be written as a to b, or a:b, or a/b. Formula: $a \\text{ to } b, \\ a:b, \\ \\frac{a}{b}$",
          "page": 25
        },
        {
          "id": "pp3u2-1:definition-2",
          "type": "definition",
          "text": "In the ratio a:b, a is called the antecedent and b the consequent; a and b together are the two terms of the ratio.",
          "page": 25
        }
      ]
    },
